Declare rules_distroless's `deb_import` reproducible so it can use the repo contents cache.

Its inputs are the sha256-pinned `.deb` URLs, the rule attributes and each dependency's
`filemap.json` (a recorded input). Without this every package repo reruns on every CI
runner, and `host_bsdtar()` reading the bsdtar binary materialises
`@bsd_tar_toolchains_linux_amd64`.

`_extracted/` holds scratch copies of `.so` linker scripts and `.pc` files that nothing in
the generated BUILD file references, so it is deleted to keep it out of the cache entry.

`deb_import` also shells out to host `grep` and `mkdir`. Their output reaches the repo
only as file lists derived from the pinned archive, so it does not affect the contents.

Not yet raised upstream.

diff --git a/apt/private/deb_import.bzl b/apt/private/deb_import.bzl
--- a/apt/private/deb_import.bzl
+++ b/apt/private/deb_import.bzl
@@ -496,6 +496,14 @@ def _deb_import_impl(rctx):
         symlink_outs = symlinks.keys(),
     ))
 
+    rctx.delete(_EXTRACT_DIR)
+
+    # Bazel <8.3.0 lacks rctx.repo_metadata
+    if not hasattr(rctx, "repo_metadata"):
+        return None
+
+    return rctx.repo_metadata(reproducible = True)
+
 deb_import = repository_rule(
     implementation = _deb_import_impl,
     attrs = {
